---
// ── Privacy Policy ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Substantive privacy policy covering the requirements for Google OAuth
// verification: explicit YouTube API scope handling, local-first data
// model, third-party services, retention, contact, etc.
//
// This is the URL submitted to Google Cloud Console under
// "OAuth consent screen → Privacy policy URL".

import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import LegalLayout from "@/components/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Tubelane"
  description="How Tubelane handles your data: local-first storage, YouTube API scope handling, third-party services, and your rights."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" updatedAt="May 7, 2026">
    <p>
      This privacy policy describes how <strong>Tubelane</strong> ("the App",
      "we", "us", "our") handles your data. Tubelane is a desktop application
      that runs locally on your computer and lets you create YouTube content
      using your own API keys for third-party AI providers.
    </p>

    <p>
      The most important thing to know up front: <strong>Tubelane is a
      local-first desktop app</strong>. We do not run servers that store your
      content. Your scripts, voiceovers, generated images, video projects,
      OAuth tokens, and API keys are stored only on your device.
    </p>

    <h2 id="data-we-collect">Data we collect</h2>

    <p>
      Tubelane itself does not transmit your usage data, telemetry, or
      content to any server we operate. Specifically:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>We do not run analytics in the desktop app.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>We do not collect telemetry.</strong> No event tracking, no crash reports sent to us.</li>
      <li><strong>We do not have a backend.</strong> There is no server-side database where your videos, scripts, or accounts are stored.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The only data we receive is:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>The email address you provide if you sign up for the private beta or contact us via email.</li>
      <li>Anonymous, aggregated traffic statistics from <code>tubelane.in</code> (server access logs and a privacy-respecting page-view counter). No cookies, no fingerprinting, no advertising trackers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="youtube-api">YouTube API and Google account access</h2>

    <p>
      Tubelane uses the <strong>YouTube Data API v3</strong> (a Google API
      service) so you can connect your YouTube channel and upload videos
      directly from the desktop app. We follow the
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/youtube/terms/developer-policies">YouTube API Services Developer Policies</a>
      and the
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Scopes we request</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.readonly</code> — read-only access to your channel info, video list, and statistics. Used to display your channel inside the app and let you pick which channel to publish to.</li>
      <li><code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.upload</code> — upload videos to YouTube on your behalf when you explicitly press the Upload button.</li>
      <li><code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube</code> — manage your videos (set thumbnails, schedule, change privacy). Used only when you take an explicit action that needs it (e.g. uploading a custom thumbnail).</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>How OAuth tokens are stored</h3>

    <p>
      When you sign in with Google, we receive an OAuth access token and
      refresh token from Google. These tokens are stored
      <strong>only on your device</strong>, in the standard application data
      directory:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>macOS: <code>~/Library/Application Support/com.tubelane.desktop/yt_tokens.json</code></li>
      <li>Windows: <code>%APPDATA%\com.tubelane.desktop\yt_tokens.json</code></li>
      <li>Linux: <code>~/.local/share/com.tubelane.desktop/yt_tokens.json</code></li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The tokens never leave your device. We do not have a server that ever
      sees, transmits, or stores them. You can revoke Tubelane's access at
      any time from your
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google account
      permissions page</a>, or by deleting the file above and disconnecting
      the channel inside the app.
    </p>

    <h3>Limited use disclosure</h3>

    <p>
      Tubelane's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs
      to any other app will adhere to the
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy#limited-use">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
      including the Limited Use requirements. We do <strong>not</strong>:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Use Google user data for serving advertisements.</li>
      <li>Sell, transfer, or share Google user data with third parties.</li>
      <li>Allow humans to read Google user data, except (a) with your explicit consent, (b) for security purposes, (c) to comply with applicable law, or (d) where the data has been aggregated and anonymized.</li>
      <li>Use the data for any purpose other than providing the features of the app you've explicitly invoked.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="third-party-ai">Third-party AI providers</h2>

    <p>
      Tubelane sends content (your scripts, prompts, audio) to third-party
      AI providers using <strong>your own API keys</strong>. We act only as
      a client. We never proxy these requests through our servers.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Anthropic (Claude)</strong> — script generation, scene planning, image prompts. <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy">Anthropic Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><strong>Google (Gemini, Imagen, Cloud TTS, Speech-to-Text)</strong> — visuals, voice synthesis, transcription. <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><strong>OpenAI (gpt-image-1, DALL·E 3, Whisper)</strong> — visuals and transcription, when selected. <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy">OpenAI Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><strong>ElevenLabs</strong> — voice synthesis, when selected. <a href="https://elevenlabs.io/privacy">ElevenLabs Privacy Policy</a></li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Each provider's data handling, retention, and training-on-input
      policies are governed by their own terms. You decide which providers
      to use by adding (or not adding) their API keys in
      <strong>Settings</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="local-storage">Data stored on your device</h2>

    <p>
      Tubelane saves the following on your computer (in the application
      data directory listed above):
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Your settings (selected providers, model preferences, channel info)</li>
      <li>API keys you enter (stored on disk; please use OS-level disk encryption)</li>
      <li>Your scripts, generated voiceovers, generated images, and video projects</li>
      <li>OAuth tokens for connected YouTube channels</li>
      <li>Local Whisper / Chatterbox model files (downloaded once on first use)</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      None of this is transmitted to us. It stays on your device until you
      delete it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="retention">Data retention and deletion</h2>

    <p>
      Because we do not run servers that store your content, retention is
      entirely under your control. To delete data created by Tubelane:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Per-video</strong>: delete the video from the Videos page inside the app.</li>
      <li><strong>All app data</strong>: delete the application data directory listed in the YouTube section above.</li>
      <li><strong>Disconnect Google</strong>: revoke at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a> or remove the channel inside Tubelane.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The only data we retain on our side is your beta-signup email, until
      you ask us to delete it (see Contact below).
    </p>

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and tracking</h2>

    <p>
      The marketing website at <strong>tubelane.in</strong> does not use
      tracking cookies, advertising pixels, or third-party trackers. We may
      use a privacy-respecting analytics service (Plausible / Umami /
      Fathom) that does not set cookies and does not collect personal data.
      The desktop app does not use cookies at all.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">Children's privacy</h2>

    <p>
      Tubelane is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly
      collect data from children. If you believe a child has provided us
      personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>

    <p>
      We may update this policy as the app evolves. Material changes will
      be reflected on this page and dated above. Continued use of the app
      after a change constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>

    <p>
      For privacy questions, data deletion requests, or to revoke beta
      access, email
      <a href="mailto:hello@tubelane.in">hello@tubelane.in</a>.
    </p>
  </LegalLayout>
</Base>
